// bubbler profile: mpv
//
// `wayland` is the display it draws on, and the only one: there is no
// `x11` beside it, so a `--vo` with no Wayland backend (`xv`, and the
// X11 fallbacks the Arch wiki names under Mpv#Fix jerky playback and
// tearing) has nothing to open.
//
// `dri` is the GPU. mpv "defaults to using the OpenGL video output
// device setting on hardware that supports it", and `--hwdec` decodes
// through the same driver (Arch wiki, Mpv). Bare, not `kms=#true`: the
// render node is what a driver draws through, and the card node is the
// display controller, which a player never opens.
//
// `pipewire` is the sound: on a PipeWire host mpv's own default audio
// output driver is `pipewire` (Arch wiki, Mpv#Screen sharing cannot
// capture audio from mpv), so this is the socket it reaches for. It
// carries capture as well as playback, so it is the microphone too;
// `pulseaudio` beside it is the same reach through the older protocol,
// not a narrower one.
//
// `home-share "Videos"` is read-only, because a player reads its files
// and writes none. Edit the node for the directory you keep films in;
// a library on another disk is named explicitly, e.g.
//   path-share "/mnt/films"
//
// No nested user namespaces: mpv nests no sandbox of its own, so the door a
// nested user namespace opens stays shut.
//
// `lint` answers `note[command-not-found]` on a host that has no mpv:
// that is the host's answer and not this profile's, which is written for
// software you may not have installed yet.
wayland
dri
pipewire
home-share "Videos"
userns "disable"
command "mpv"
